PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L01U1.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":1,"cefr":"A1a","unit":1,"theme":"Hello, Friends!","essential_question":"How do we tell people who we are?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS1","title":"Meet the Class: am, is, are","objectives":["Students will be able to use am, is and are with I, you, he, she, it, we and they.","Students will be able to find am, is and are in a short text.","I can say who I am with am, is and are.","I can find am, is and are in a story."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام am وis وare مع الضمائر.","سيتمكن الطلاب من إيجاد am وis وare في نص قصير.","أستطيع أن أعرّف بنفسي باستخدام am وis وare.","أستطيع أن أجد am وis وare في قصة."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"hello","pos":"interjection","ipa":"/həˈloʊ/","definition":"a word you say when you meet someone","arabic":"مرحبًا","example":"Hello! Welcome to our class.","image_id":"GV-L01-U1-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U1-LS1-W01"},{"word":"name","pos":"noun","ipa":"/neɪm/","definition":"the word people call you","arabic":"اسم","example":"Her name is Noura.","image_id":"GV-L01-U1-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U1-LS1-W02"},{"word":"friend","pos":"noun","ipa":"/frɛnd/","definition":"a person you like and play with","arabic":"صديق","example":"Faisal is a good friend.","image_id":"GV-L01-U1-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U1-LS1-W03"},{"word":"happy","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈhæpi/","definition":"feeling good; smiling","arabic":"سعيد","example":"The happy boy is laughing.","image_id":"GV-L01-U1-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U1-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"We use the verb be to say who we are, how old we are and how we feel. In the present, be has three forms: am, is and are.\nLook at the subject (the person or thing at the start). The subject tells you which form to use.\nI → am: I am Omar.\nhe, she, it, one person or one thing → is: Yusuf is my friend.\nyou, we, they, two or more people or things → are: We are friends.\nShort forms: I'm, you're, he's, she's, it's, we're, they're.","examples":["I am Omar.","You are my classmate.","Sara is eight years old.","Mr. Khalid is our English teacher.","The cat is small and white.","We are in Class 3A.","Lina and Noura are cousins.","They're happy today."],"common_errors":["✗ He teacher. → ✓ He is a teacher. (Arabic says هو معلم with no verb, but English needs is.)","✗ I have nine years. → ✓ I am nine years old. (English uses be for age.)","✗ They is happy. → ✓ They are happy. (They means more than one, so we use are.)"],"arabic":"نستخدم الفعل be للتعريف بأنفسنا وبالآخرين، وللتعبير عن العمر والمشاعر.\nالضمير I يأخذ am، والضمائر he وshe وit والمفرد تأخذ is، والضمائر you وwe وthey والجمع تأخذ are.\nفي العربية نقول «هو معلم» بدون فعل، لكن في الإنجليزية لا بد من is: He is a teacher.\nللعمر نستخدم am/is/are وليس have: I am nine years old."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Meet the Class: am, is, are”. Let’s learn the verb be (am, is, are) together.","on_screen":"GV-L01-U1-LS1 | Meet the Class: am, is, are","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “First Day at School”: Hello! My name is Omar. Look at the green words.","on_screen":"Hello! My name is Omar.","visual":"Image GV-L01-U1-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"We use the verb be to say who we are, how old we are and how we feel. In the present, be has three forms: am, is and are. Look at the subject (the person or thing at the start). The subject tells you which form to use.","on_screen":"I → am: I am Omar. • he, she, it, one person or one thing → is: Yusuf is my friend. • you, we, they, two or more people or things → are: We are friends.","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. I am Omar. You are my classmate. Sara is eight years old.","on_screen":"I am Omar. / You are my classmate. / Sara is eight years old.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “He teacher.” That’s not right. We say: “He is a teacher.”","on_screen":"✗ He teacher.   ✓ He is a teacher.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: In \"Yusuf is my friend\", is Yusuf one person or two? … Think! … One person – so we use *is*. Great job! Now you can say: I can say who I am with am, is and are.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say who I am with am, is and are.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: the verb be (am, is, are).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نستخدم الفعل be للتعريف بأنفسنا وبالآخرين، وللتعبير عن العمر والمشاعر.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: He teacher. — الصحيح: He is a teacher.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أعرّف بنفسي باستخدام am وis وare."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"First Day at School","body":"Hello! My name is Omar. I am nine years old.\nThis is Mr. Khalid. He is our teacher. He is kind.\nThis is Yusuf. He is my friend. We are in Class 3A.\nYusuf is happy today. I am happy too!\nOur classroom is big. It is nice and bright.\nWe are ready to learn!","word_count":55,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U1-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"I ___ ready for school.","options":["am","is","are","be"],"answer":"am","explanation":"Use am with I.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم am مع I فقط."},{"q":"Yusuf ___ in the classroom.","options":["are","am","be","is"],"answer":"is","explanation":"Use is with he, she, it or one person or thing.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم is مع he وshe وit أو مع المفرد."},{"q":"We ___ good friends.","options":["am","be","is","are"],"answer":"are","explanation":"Use are with you, we, they or two or more people or things.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم are مع you وwe وthey أو مع الجمع."},{"q":"My bag ___ blue.","options":["am","are","is","be"],"answer":"is","explanation":"Use is with he, she, it or one person or thing.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم is مع he وshe وit أو مع المفرد."},{"q":"You ___ a great helper.","options":["are","be","am","is"],"answer":"are","explanation":"Use are with you, we, they or two or more people or things.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم are مع you وwe وthey أو مع الجمع."},{"q":"Adam and Yusuf ___ in the garden.","options":["be","are","is","am"],"answer":"are","explanation":"Use are with you, we, they or two or more people or things.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم are مع you وwe وthey أو مع الجمع."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS1-B1","type":"order","instructions":"Guided practice: Put the words in order.","items":[{"q":"years old / am / eight / I   ( . )","options":["years old","am","eight","I"],"answer":"I am eight years old.","explanation":"Word order: Use am with I.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الكلمات: نستخدم am مع I فقط."},{"q":"is / sister / She / my   ( . )","options":["is","sister","She","my"],"answer":"She is my sister.","explanation":"Word order: Use is with he, she, it or one person or thing.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الكلمات: نستخدم is مع he وshe وit أو مع المفرد."},{"q":"today / We / are / happy   ( . )","options":["today","We","are","happy"],"answer":"We are happy today.","explanation":"Word order: Use are with you, we, they or two or more people or things.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الكلمات: نستخدم are مع you وwe وthey أو مع الجمع."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS1-B2","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Complete with am, is or are. Word bank: am, are, is","items":[{"q":"The teacher ______ in the library.","options":[],"answer":"is","explanation":"Use is with he, she, it or one person or thing.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم is مع he وshe وit أو مع المفرد."},{"q":"My friends ______ at the park.","options":[],"answer":"are","explanation":"Use are with you, we, they or two or more people or things.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم are مع you وwe وthey أو مع الجمع."},{"q":"I ______ very hungry.","options":[],"answer":"am","explanation":"Use am with I.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم am مع I فقط."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Complete the sentences about you.","items":[{"q":"My name ___.","options":[],"answer":"My name is Faisal.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the verb be (am, is, are) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I ___ ___ years old.","options":[],"answer":"I am ten years old.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the verb be (am, is, are) correctly and makes sense. Use be (am/is/are) for age, not have.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح. نستخدم be للعمر وليس have."},{"q":"My best friend ___ ___.","options":[],"answer":"My best friend is Adam.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the verb be (am, is, are) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Today I ___ ___. (happy / tired / hungry)","options":[],"answer":"Today I am happy.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the verb be (am, is, are) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"My teacher ___ ___.","options":[],"answer":"My teacher is kind.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the verb be (am, is, are) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write about you and your class.","items":[{"q":"Write 3 sentences about you. Use I am.","options":[],"answer":"I am Faisal. I am nine years old. I am happy today.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the verb be (am, is, are) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences about a friend. Use He is or She is.","options":[],"answer":"He is Majed. He is funny.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the verb be (am, is, are) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Draw your class. Write 2 sentences with We are.","options":[],"answer":"We are in Class 3B. We are friends.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the verb be (am, is, are) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Ball Toss Sentences","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["Students stand in a circle. The teacher says a cue word and throws the ball.","The catcher makes a sentence with the cue word and the verb be (am, is, are).","If it is correct, the catcher chooses the next cue word and throws the ball to a new student.","If it is not correct, classmates help fix it, and the same student tries again."],"data":[{"label":"I"},{"label":"you"},{"label":"Omar"},{"label":"Sara"},{"label":"we"},{"label":"they"},{"label":"Mr. Khalid"},{"label":"my friends"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"I ___ a student.","options":["is","am","be","are"],"answer":"am","explanation":"Use am with I.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم am مع I فقط."},{"q":"It ___ a cat.","options":["are","be","is","am"],"answer":"is","explanation":"Use is with he, she, it or one person or thing.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم is مع he وshe وit أو مع المفرد."},{"q":"They ___ my brothers.","options":["are","is","am","be"],"answer":"are","explanation":"Use are with you, we, they or two or more people or things.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم are مع you وwe وthey أو مع الجمع."},{"q":"Reem ___ seven years old.","options":["has","are","is","am"],"answer":"is","explanation":"Use be (am/is/are) for age, not have.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم be للعمر وليس have."},{"q":"We ___ at home now.","options":["is","am","are","be"],"answer":"are","explanation":"Use are with you, we, they or two or more people or things.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم are مع you وwe وthey أو مع الجمع."},{"q":"","options":["He are my teacher.","He my teacher.","He am my teacher.","He is my teacher."],"answer":"He is my teacher.","explanation":"An English sentence needs a verb: add am, is or are.","explanation_ar":"الجملة الإنجليزية تحتاج فعلًا؛ أضف am أو is أو are."},{"q":"Adam and I ___ in the same class.","options":["am","are","be","is"],"answer":"are","explanation":"Use are with you, we, they or two or more people or things.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم are مع you وwe وthey أو مع الجمع."},{"q":"She is happy. → Choose the short form.","options":["She're happy.","She's happy.","She'is happy.","Shes happy."],"answer":"She's happy.","explanation":"Use is with he, she, it or one person or thing.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم is مع he وshe وit أو مع المفرد."},{"q":"The pencils ___ on the desk.","options":["be","is","am","are"],"answer":"are","explanation":"Use are with you, we, they or two or more people or things.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم are مع you وwe وthey أو مع الجمع."},{"q":"","options":["My brother is seven years old.","My brother has seven years.","My brother are seven years old.","My brother seven years old."],"answer":"My brother is seven years old.","explanation":"Use be (am/is/are) for age, not have.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم be للعمر وليس have."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"Omar and Yusuf smiling at their desks in a bright Grade 3 classroom while Mr. Khalid waves hello on the first day of school. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Omar and Yusuf smiling at their desks in a bright Grade 3 classroom while Mr. Khalid waves hello on the first day of school"},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about the verb be (am, is, are), with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about the verb be (am, is, are), with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right"},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows hello (a word you say when you meet someone); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing hello: a word you say when you meet someone"},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows name (the word people call you); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing name: the word people call you"},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows friend (a person you like and play with); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing friend: a person you like and play with"},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows happy (feeling good; smiling); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing happy: feeling good; smiling"},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Ball Toss Sentences”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Ball Toss Sentences"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U1-LS1-W01","script":"hello. hello. Hello! Welcome to our class.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U1-LS1-W02","script":"name. name. Her name is Noura.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U1-LS1-W03","script":"friend. friend. Faisal is a good friend.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U1-LS1-W04","script":"happy. happy. The happy boy is laughing.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U1-LS1-T1","script":"Hello! My name is Omar. I am nine years old. This is Mr. Khalid. He is our teacher. He is kind. This is Yusuf. He is my friend. We are in Class 3A. Yusuf is happy today. I am happy too! Our classroom is big. It is nice and bright. We are ready to learn!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U1-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Meet the Class: am, is, are”. Let’s learn the verb be (am, is, are) together. Listen to the start of “First Day at School”: Hello! My name is Omar. Look at the green words. We use the verb be to say who we are, how old we are and how we feel. In the present, be has three forms: am, is and are. Look at the subject (the person or thing at the start). The subject tells you which form to use. Here are some examples. I am Omar. You are my classmate. Sara is eight years old. Be careful! Some learners say: “He teacher.” That’s not right. We say: “He is a teacher.” Quick check: In \"Yusuf is my friend\", is Yusuf one person or two? … Think! … One person – so we use *is*. Great job! Now you can say: I can say who I am with am, is and are.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS2","title":"Is it…? Are you…? Questions and Answers","objectives":["Students will be able to make negative sentences with am not, isn't and aren't.","Students will be able to ask and answer yes/no questions with be.","I can say what is not true with isn't, aren't and I'm not.","I can ask \"Are you…?\" and answer \"Yes, I am.\" or \"No, I'm not.\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تكوين جمل منفية باستخدام am not وisn't وaren't.","سيتمكن الطلاب من طرح أسئلة نعم/لا والإجابة عنها باستخدام be.","أستطيع أن أنفي باستخدام isn't وaren't وI'm not.","أستطيع أن أسأل Are you…? وأجيب Yes, I am أو No, I'm not."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"sad","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/sæd/","definition":"feeling bad; you want to cry","arabic":"حزين","example":"The girl is sad because it is raining.","image_id":"GV-L01-U1-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U1-LS2-W01"},{"word":"tired","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈtaɪɚd/","definition":"you want to rest or sleep","arabic":"متعب","example":"Dad is tired after work.","image_id":"GV-L01-U1-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U1-LS2-W02"},{"word":"teacher","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈtitʃɚ/","definition":"a person who helps you learn at school","arabic":"معلم","example":"Our teacher reads us a story.","image_id":"GV-L01-U1-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U1-LS2-W03"},{"word":"student","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈstudənt/","definition":"a person who learns at school","arabic":"طالب","example":"Every student has a new book.","image_id":"GV-L01-U1-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U1-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"To make a negative, put not after am, is or are. We often use short forms: I'm not, isn't, aren't.\nTo make a question, move am, is or are to the start: You are tired. → Are you tired?\nShort answers use the same verb: Yes, I am. / No, he isn't.","examples":["I'm not tired today.","Omar isn't hungry.","We aren't late.","Is Lina your sister? – Yes, she is.","Are they in the garden? – No, they aren't.","Am I next? – Yes, you are.","The window isn't open.","Is it cold? – No, it isn't."],"common_errors":["✗ He not happy. → ✓ He isn't happy. (Arabic uses ليس alone; English needs is + not.)","✗ You are hungry? → ✓ Are you hungry? (In a question, are comes first.)","✗ Yes, I'm. → ✓ Yes, I am. (No short form at the end of a positive short answer.)","✗ I amn't sad. → ✓ I'm not sad. (There is no word \"amn't\".)"],"arabic":"للنفي نضع not بعد am أو is أو are: She is not tired، والاختصار: isn't / aren't / I'm not.\nللسؤال نقدّم am أو is أو are إلى بداية الجملة: Are you tired?\nالإجابة القصيرة: Yes, I am. / No, I'm not. ولا نقول Yes, I'm."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Is it…? Are you…? Questions and Answers”. Let’s learn be in negatives and yes/no questions together.","on_screen":"GV-L01-U1-LS2 | Is it…? Are you…? Questions and Answers","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: She is tired. She is not tired. → She isn't tired. Is she tired? – Yes, she is. / No, she isn't.","on_screen":"She is tired. | She is not tired. → She isn't tired. | Is she tired? – Yes, she is. / No, she isn't.","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"To make a negative, put not after am, is or are. We often use short forms: I'm not, isn't, aren't. To make a question, move am, is or are to the start: You are tired. → Are you tired?","on_screen":"be in negatives and yes/no questions","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. I'm not tired today. Omar isn't hungry. We aren't late.","on_screen":"I'm not tired today. / Omar isn't hungry. / We aren't late.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “He not happy.” That’s not right. We say: “He isn't happy.”","on_screen":"✗ He not happy.   ✓ He isn't happy.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"Omar isn't hungry.\" Does Omar want food now? … Think! … No, he doesn't. Great job! Now you can say: I can say what is not true with isn't, aren't and I'm not.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say what is not true with isn't, aren't and I'm not.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: be in negatives and yes/no questions.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","للنفي نضع not بعد am أو is أو are: She is not tired، والاختصار: isn't / aren't / I'm not.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: He not happy. — الصحيح: He isn't happy.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أنفي باستخدام isn't وaren't وI'm not."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"Sara ___ sad. She is happy.","options":["isn't","am not","not","aren't"],"answer":"isn't","explanation":"Negative: am / is / are + not (I'm not, isn't, aren't).","explanation_ar":"النفي: am أو is أو are ثم not."},{"q":"We ___ at home. We are at school.","options":["am not","isn't","aren't","not"],"answer":"aren't","explanation":"Negative: am / is / are + not (I'm not, isn't, aren't).","explanation_ar":"النفي: am أو is أو are ثم not."},{"q":"___ you ready?","options":["Is","Be","Am","Are"],"answer":"Are","explanation":"Question: put am, is or are first.","explanation_ar":"السؤال: نبدأ بـ am أو is أو are."},{"q":"___ Mr. Khalid in the office?","options":["Am","Is","Be","Are"],"answer":"Is","explanation":"Question: put am, is or are first.","explanation_ar":"السؤال: نبدأ بـ am أو is أو are."},{"q":"Is it a pencil? – Yes, it ___.","options":["isn't","is","are","it's"],"answer":"is","explanation":"Short answers repeat the verb: Yes, she is. / No, she isn't.","explanation_ar":"الإجابة القصيرة تكرر الفعل."},{"q":"Are you thirsty? – No, ___.","options":["I amn't","I aren't","I isn't","I'm not"],"answer":"I'm not","explanation":"Short answers repeat the verb: Yes, she is. / No, she isn't.","explanation_ar":"الإجابة القصيرة تكرر الفعل."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS2-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Change the sentences. Follow the word in brackets.","items":[{"q":"Adam is in the garden.  (negative)","options":[],"answer":"Adam isn't in the garden.","explanation":"Negative: am / is / are + not (I'm not, isn't, aren't).","explanation_ar":"النفي: am أو is أو are ثم not."},{"q":"The books are new.  (negative)","options":[],"answer":"The books aren't new.","explanation":"Negative: am / is / are + not (I'm not, isn't, aren't).","explanation_ar":"النفي: am أو is أو are ثم not."},{"q":"I am cold.  (negative)","options":[],"answer":"I'm not cold.","explanation":"Negative: am / is / are + not (I'm not, isn't, aren't).","explanation_ar":"النفي: am أو is أو are ثم not."},{"q":"Lina is nine.  (question)","options":[],"answer":"Is Lina nine?","explanation":"Question: put am, is or are first.","explanation_ar":"السؤال: نبدأ بـ am أو is أو are."},{"q":"They are in Class 3B.  (question)","options":[],"answer":"Are they in Class 3B?","explanation":"Question: put am, is or are first.","explanation_ar":"السؤال: نبدأ بـ am أو is أو are."},{"q":"The cat is under the bed.  (question)","options":[],"answer":"Is the cat under the bed?","explanation":"Question: put am, is or are first.","explanation_ar":"السؤال: نبدأ بـ am أو is أو are."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Answer about you. Use short answers.","items":[{"q":"Are you nine years old?","options":[],"answer":"Yes, I am. / No, I'm not.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses be in negatives and yes/no questions correctly and makes sense. Short answers repeat the verb: Yes, she is. / No, she isn't.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح. الإجابة القصيرة تكرر الفعل."},{"q":"Is your teacher tall?","options":[],"answer":"Yes, he is. / No, he isn't.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses be in negatives and yes/no questions correctly and makes sense. Short answers repeat the verb: Yes, she is. / No, she isn't.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح. الإجابة القصيرة تكرر الفعل."},{"q":"Are you hungry now?","options":[],"answer":"No, I'm not.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses be in negatives and yes/no questions correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Is your bag red?","options":[],"answer":"Yes, it is. / No, it isn't.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses be in negatives and yes/no questions correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Are your friends in your class?","options":[],"answer":"Yes, they are.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses be in negatives and yes/no questions correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Ask, answer and write.","items":[{"q":"Write 3 questions for your partner with Are you…?","options":[],"answer":"Are you tired? Are you happy? Are you ten?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses be in negatives and yes/no questions correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences that are NOT true about you. Use isn't, aren't or I'm not.","options":[],"answer":"I'm not hungry. My bag isn't big.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses be in negatives and yes/no questions correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask your partner your questions. Write his answers.","options":[],"answer":"Yes, he is. / No, he isn't.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses be in negatives and yes/no questions correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Dice Sentences","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["Turn over a cue card and roll the die.","Make a sentence with the cue in the form shown by the die.","The player on the left checks; a correct sentence wins the card.","The player with the most cards after 7 minutes wins."],"data":[{"cue":"he / happy / +"},{"cue":"they / sad / –"},{"cue":"you / ten / ?"},{"cue":"I / tired / +"},{"cue":"we / friends / +"},{"cue":"she / hungry / –"},{"cue":"Omar / at school / ?"},{"cue":"it / a cat / +"},{"cue":"Lina and Sara / sisters / ?"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"The door ___ open. It is closed.","options":["not","am not","isn't","aren't"],"answer":"isn't","explanation":"Negative: am / is / are + not (I'm not, isn't, aren't).","explanation_ar":"النفي: am أو is أو are ثم not."},{"q":"___ they your friends?","options":["Is","Are","Am","Do"],"answer":"Are","explanation":"Question: put am, is or are first.","explanation_ar":"السؤال: نبدأ بـ am أو is أو are."},{"q":"Is Omar in Class 3A? – Yes, he ___.","options":["are","is","isn't","he's"],"answer":"is","explanation":"Short answers repeat the verb: Yes, she is. / No, she isn't.","explanation_ar":"الإجابة القصيرة تكرر الفعل."},{"q":"I ___ sleepy. I am wide awake.","options":["is not","not am","are not","am not"],"answer":"am not","explanation":"Negative: am / is / are + not (I'm not, isn't, aren't).","explanation_ar":"النفي: am أو is أو are ثم not."},{"q":"___ your sister at home?","options":["Be","Is","Are","Am"],"answer":"Is","explanation":"Question: put am, is or are first.","explanation_ar":"السؤال: نبدأ بـ am أو is أو are."},{"q":"Are the boys in the park? – No, they ___.","options":["aren't","are","isn't","not"],"answer":"aren't","explanation":"Short answers repeat the verb: Yes, she is. / No, she isn't.","explanation_ar":"الإجابة القصيرة تكرر الفعل."},{"q":"","options":["She is your cousin?","Are she your cousin?","Is your cousin she?","Is she your cousin?"],"answer":"Is she your cousin?","explanation":"Question: put am, is or are first.","explanation_ar":"السؤال: نبدأ بـ am أو is أو are."},{"q":"Are you ten? – ___","options":["Yes, I is.","Yes, I'm.","Yes, I am.","Yes, am I."],"answer":"Yes, I am.","explanation":"Positive short answers use the full form: Yes, I am.","explanation_ar":"الإجابة القصيرة بالإيجاب لا تُختصر."},{"q":"","options":["We aren't late.","We amn't late.","We isn't late.","We not late."],"answer":"We aren't late.","explanation":"Negative: am / is / are + not (I'm not, isn't, aren't).","explanation_ar":"النفي: am أو is أو are ثم not."},{"q":"","options":["Is it hot? – No, it aren't.","Are it hot? – No, it isn't.","Is it hot? – No, it isn't.","Is it hot? – No, it not."],"answer":"Is it hot? – No, it isn't.","explanation":"Short answers repeat the verb: Yes, she is. / No, she isn't.","explanation_ar":"الإجابة القصيرة تكرر الفعل."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"Sara and Lina playing a guessing game with picture cards in the school library, one girl asking a question with a thought bubble. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Sara and Lina playing a guessing game with picture cards in the school library, one girl asking a question with a thought bubble"},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of be in negatives and yes/no questions: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Hello, Friends!”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of be in negatives and yes/no questions: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Hello, Friends!”"},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows sad (feeling bad; you want to cry); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing sad: feeling bad; you want to cry"},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows tired (you want to rest or sleep); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing tired: you want to rest or sleep"},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows teacher (a person who helps you learn at school); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing teacher: a person who helps you learn at school"},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows student (a person who learns at school); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing student: a person who learns at school"},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Dice Sentences”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Dice Sentences"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U1-LS2-W01","script":"sad. sad. The girl is sad because it is raining.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U1-LS2-W02","script":"tired. tired. Dad is tired after work.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U1-LS2-W03","script":"teacher. teacher. Our teacher reads us a story.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U1-LS2-W04","script":"student. student. Every student has a new book.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U1-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Is it…? Are you…? Questions and Answers”. Let’s learn be in negatives and yes/no questions together. Remember these patterns: She is tired. She is not tired. → She isn't tired. Is she tired? – Yes, she is. / No, she isn't. To make a negative, put not after am, is or are. We often use short forms: I'm not, isn't, aren't. To make a question, move am, is or are to the start: You are tired. → Are you tired? Here are some examples. I'm not tired today. Omar isn't hungry. We aren't late. Be careful! Some learners say: “He not happy.” That’s not right. We say: “He isn't happy.” Quick check: \"Omar isn't hungry.\" Does Omar want food now? … Think! … No, he doesn't. Great job! Now you can say: I can say what is not true with isn't, aren't and I'm not.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS3","title":"How Do You Feel? Feelings and Greetings","objectives":["Students will be able to name and use feeling words after am, is and are.","Students will be able to match opposites and choose the right greeting for the time of day.","I can say how I feel.","I can greet people at different times of the day."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تسمية كلمات المشاعر واستخدامها بعد am وis وare.","سيتمكن الطلاب من مطابقة الأضداد واختيار التحية المناسبة لوقت اليوم.","أستطيع أن أعبّر عن مشاعري.","أستطيع أن أحيّي الناس في أوقات اليوم المختلفة."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"hungry","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈhʌŋɡri/","definition":"you want to eat","arabic":"جائع","example":"The hungry cat wants some fish.","image_id":"GV-L01-U1-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U1-LS3-W01"},{"word":"excited","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ɪkˈsaɪtəd/","definition":"very happy because something fun is coming","arabic":"متحمس","example":"The boys are excited about the match.","image_id":"GV-L01-U1-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U1-LS3-W02"},{"word":"goodbye","pos":"interjection","ipa":"/ˌɡʊdˈbaɪ/","definition":"what you say when you go away","arabic":"مع السلامة","example":"Say goodbye to Grandma.","image_id":"GV-L01-U1-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U1-LS3-W03"},{"word":"classmate","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈklæˌsmeɪt/","definition":"a person in the same class as you","arabic":"زميل الصف","example":"My classmate shares his crayons.","image_id":"GV-L01-U1-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U1-LS3-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Feeling words tell us how someone is: happy, sad, tired, hungry, excited. We use them after am, is or are: I am hungry.\nMany words have an opposite: happy ↔ sad, hello ↔ goodbye. Learning words in pairs helps you remember them.\nWe greet people in different ways at different times of the day.\nCollocations/phrases: happy ↔ sad • hungry ↔ full • excited ↔ bored • hello ↔ goodbye | Good morning (before 12 o'clock) • Good afternoon (after 12) • Good evening (after sunset) | Nice to meet you. – Nice to meet you, too. • See you tomorrow!","examples":["I am hungry. Can I have a sandwich?","Lina is excited about the school trip.","Goodbye, Mr. Khalid! See you tomorrow.","Yusuf is my classmate. We sit together.","Omar is tired after football.","The baby is sad because her toy is broken.","Good morning, everyone!","Nice to meet you, Adam."],"common_errors":["✗ I am boring in the lesson. → ✓ I am bored in the lesson. (bored = how you feel; boring = how the lesson is.)","✗ Good night! (when you arrive in the evening) → ✓ Good evening! (Say Good night only when you leave at night or go to bed.)","✗ Bye bye, teacher. → ✓ Goodbye, Mr. Khalid. (At school, use Goodbye and the teacher's name.)"],"arabic":"كلمات المشاعر تأتي بعد am أو is أو are: I am hungry (أنا جائع).\nتعلّم الكلمات مع أضدادها: happy (سعيد) ↔ sad (حزين).\nنقول Good evening عند اللقاء مساءً، وGood night عند الوداع ليلًا أو عند النوم فقط.\nbored تعني «أشعر بالملل»، أمّا boring فتعني «ممل» وتصف الشيء."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “How Do You Feel? Feelings and Greetings”. Let’s learn feeling words, opposites and greetings together.","on_screen":"GV-L01-U1-LS3 | How Do You Feel? Feelings and Greetings","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. hungry: you want to eat. excited: very happy because something fun is coming. goodbye: what you say when you go away.","on_screen":"hungry | excited | goodbye","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Feeling words tell us how someone is: happy, sad, tired, hungry, excited. We use them after am, is or are: I am hungry. Many words have an opposite: happy ↔ sad, hello ↔ goodbye. Learning words in pairs helps you remember them.","on_screen":"feeling words, opposites and greetings","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. I am hungry. Can I have a sandwich? Lina is excited about the school trip. Goodbye, Mr. Khalid! See you tomorrow.","on_screen":"I am hungry. Can I have a sandwich? / Lina is excited about the school trip. / Goodbye, Mr. Khalid! See you tomorrow.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I am boring in the lesson.” That’s not right. We say: “I am bored in the lesson.” bored = how you feel; boring = how the lesson is.","on_screen":"✗ I am boring in the lesson.   ✓ I am bored in the lesson.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: When do we say \"Good night\"? … Think! … When we leave at night or go to bed. Great job! Now you can say: I can say how I feel.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say how I feel.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: feeling words, opposites and greetings.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","كلمات المشاعر تأتي بعد am أو is أو are: I am hungry (أنا جائع).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I am boring in the lesson. — الصحيح: I am bored in the lesson.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أعبّر عن مشاعري."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"happy ↔ ___","options":["excited","sad","hungry","nice"],"answer":"sad","explanation":"Opposites have opposite meanings (happy ↔ sad).","explanation_ar":"الأضداد كلمات معناها عكسي."},{"q":"hello ↔ ___","options":["please","thank you","goodbye","good morning"],"answer":"goodbye","explanation":"Opposites have opposite meanings (happy ↔ sad).","explanation_ar":"الأضداد كلمات معناها عكسي."},{"q":"hungry ↔ ___","options":["full","excited","tired","sad"],"answer":"full","explanation":"Opposites have opposite meanings (happy ↔ sad).","explanation_ar":"الأضداد كلمات معناها عكسي."},{"q":"excited ↔ ___","options":["happy","friendly","bored","hungry"],"answer":"bored","explanation":"Opposites have opposite meanings (happy ↔ sad).","explanation_ar":"الأضداد كلمات معناها عكسي."},{"q":"It is 8 o'clock in the morning. You say: \"___, Mr. Khalid!\"","options":["Good night","Good evening","Goodbye","Good morning"],"answer":"Good morning","explanation":"Choose the greeting that matches the time of day or the situation.","explanation_ar":"اختر التحية المناسبة للوقت أو الموقف."},{"q":"You meet Adam for the first time. You say:","options":["Good night.","Nice to meet you.","See you tomorrow.","I'm tired."],"answer":"Nice to meet you.","explanation":"Choose the greeting that matches the time of day or the situation.","explanation_ar":"اختر التحية المناسبة للوقت أو الموقف."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the word to the sentence.","items":[{"q":"hungry","options":["I say it when I go home.","I want to eat now.","My fish is ill. I want to cry.","I want to sleep.","He sits next to me in class.","Yay! The trip is tomorrow!"],"answer":"I want to eat now.","explanation":"hungry → I want to eat now.. Think about the meaning of the feeling word in the sentence.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في معنى كلمة الشعور في الجملة."},{"q":"tired","options":["I say it when I go home.","I want to eat now.","My fish is ill. I want to cry.","I want to sleep.","He sits next to me in class.","Yay! The trip is tomorrow!"],"answer":"I want to sleep.","explanation":"tired → I want to sleep.. Think about the meaning of the feeling word in the sentence.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في معنى كلمة الشعور في الجملة."},{"q":"excited","options":["I say it when I go home.","I want to eat now.","My fish is ill. I want to cry.","I want to sleep.","He sits next to me in class.","Yay! The trip is tomorrow!"],"answer":"Yay! The trip is tomorrow!","explanation":"excited → Yay! The trip is tomorrow!. Think about the meaning of the feeling word in the sentence.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في معنى كلمة الشعور في الجملة."},{"q":"sad","options":["I say it when I go home.","I want to eat now.","My fish is ill. I want to cry.","I want to sleep.","He sits next to me in class.","Yay! The trip is tomorrow!"],"answer":"My fish is ill. I want to cry.","explanation":"sad → My fish is ill. I want to cry.. Think about the meaning of the feeling word in the sentence.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في معنى كلمة الشعور في الجملة."},{"q":"classmate","options":["I say it when I go home.","I want to eat now.","My fish is ill. I want to cry.","I want to sleep.","He sits next to me in class.","Yay! The trip is tomorrow!"],"answer":"He sits next to me in class.","explanation":"classmate → He sits next to me in class.. Think about the meaning of the feeling word in the sentence.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في معنى كلمة الشعور في الجملة."},{"q":"goodbye","options":["I say it when I go home.","I want to eat now.","My fish is ill. I want to cry.","I want to sleep.","He sits next to me in class.","Yay! The trip is tomorrow!"],"answer":"I say it when I go home.","explanation":"goodbye → I say it when I go home.. Think about the meaning of the feeling word in the sentence.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في معنى كلمة الشعور في الجملة."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Complete the sentences about you.","items":[{"q":"I am happy when ___.","options":[],"answer":"I am happy when I play football.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses feeling words, opposites and greetings correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I am tired after ___.","options":[],"answer":"I am tired after swimming.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses feeling words, opposites and greetings correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I am hungry at ___ o'clock.","options":[],"answer":"I am hungry at one o'clock.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses feeling words, opposites and greetings correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I am excited about ___.","options":[],"answer":"I am excited about Eid.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses feeling words, opposites and greetings correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"My classmate ___ is ___.","options":[],"answer":"My classmate Saad is funny.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses feeling words, opposites and greetings correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write and say.","items":[{"q":"Write a short card to a new classmate. Use Hello, Nice to meet you and Goodbye.","options":[],"answer":"Hello, Ali! Nice to meet you. I am Fahad. Goodbye!","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses feeling words, opposites and greetings correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Draw three faces. Write how each person feels.","options":[],"answer":"He is happy. She is tired. He is hungry.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses feeling words, opposites and greetings correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences with opposites.","options":[],"answer":"Omar is happy. Sara is sad.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses feeling words, opposites and greetings correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Vocabulary Bingo","mechanic":"matching","rules":["Students write nine words from the list in their grid.","The teacher (or a student caller) reads a definition or Arabic meaning.","Students cross out the matching word.","Three in a row = \"Bingo!\" The winner must read the words and say what each means."],"data":[{"word":"hello","match":"a word you say when you meet someone","arabic":"مرحبًا"},{"word":"name","match":"the word people call you","arabic":"اسم"},{"word":"friend","match":"a person you like and play with","arabic":"صديق"},{"word":"happy","match":"feeling good; smiling","arabic":"سعيد"},{"word":"sad","match":"feeling bad; you want to cry","arabic":"حزين"},{"word":"tired","match":"you want to rest or sleep","arabic":"متعب"},{"word":"teacher","match":"a person who helps you learn at school","arabic":"معلم"},{"word":"student","match":"a person who learns at school","arabic":"طالب"},{"word":"hungry","match":"you want to eat","arabic":"جائع"},{"word":"excited","match":"very happy because something fun is coming","arabic":"متحمس"},{"word":"goodbye","match":"what you say when you go away","arabic":"مع السلامة"},{"word":"classmate","match":"a person in the same class as you","arabic":"زميل الصف"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"I want to sleep. I am ___.","options":["happy","tired","excited","hungry"],"answer":"tired","explanation":"Think about the meaning of the feeling word in the sentence.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في معنى كلمة الشعور في الجملة."},{"q":"It is 7 p.m. You arrive at your uncle's house. You say:","options":["Goodbye!","Good morning!","Good night!","Good evening!"],"answer":"Good evening!","explanation":"Choose the greeting that matches the time of day or the situation.","explanation_ar":"اختر التحية المناسبة للوقت أو الموقف."},{"q":"The opposite of \"hello\" is ___.","options":["goodbye","hi","please","sorry"],"answer":"goodbye","explanation":"Opposites have opposite meanings (happy ↔ sad).","explanation_ar":"الأضداد كلمات معناها عكسي."},{"q":"Faisal is in my class. He is my ___.","options":["classmate","brother","teacher","cousin"],"answer":"classmate","explanation":"Think about the meaning of the feeling word in the sentence.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في معنى كلمة الشعور في الجملة."},{"q":"We have a party today! We are ___.","options":["hungry","tired","excited","sad"],"answer":"excited","explanation":"Think about the meaning of the feeling word in the sentence.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في معنى كلمة الشعور في الجملة."},{"q":"I am ___ because the film is long and slow.","options":["excited","bored","happy","boring"],"answer":"bored","explanation":"bored = the feeling; boring = the thing that makes you feel bored.","explanation_ar":"bored للشعور وboring للشيء."},{"q":"The lesson is ___. Nothing is new.","options":["hungry","boring","bored","excited"],"answer":"boring","explanation":"bored = the feeling; boring = the thing that makes you feel bored.","explanation_ar":"bored للشعور وboring للشيء."},{"q":"\"I want my lunch now!\" How does she feel?","options":["hungry","sad","bored","tired"],"answer":"hungry","explanation":"Think about the meaning of the feeling word in the sentence.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في معنى كلمة الشعور في الجملة."},{"q":"","options":["hungry – tired","hello – nice","excited – happy","happy – sad"],"answer":"happy – sad","explanation":"Opposites have opposite meanings (happy ↔ sad).","explanation_ar":"الأضداد كلمات معناها عكسي."},{"q":"","options":["Nice to meeting you, Adam.","Nice you meet, Adam.","Nice to meet you, Adam.","Nice meet you, Adam."],"answer":"Nice to meet you, Adam.","explanation":"Choose the greeting that matches the time of day or the situation.","explanation_ar":"اختر التحية المناسبة للوقت أو الموقف."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"Four children with different faces – happy, tired, hungry and excited – standing in a line at the school gate in the morning, Zaki the Falcon waving. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Four children with different faces – happy, tired, hungry and excited – standing in a line at the school gate in the morning, Zaki the Falcon waving"},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 4 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 4 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows hungry (you want to eat); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing hungry: you want to eat"},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows excited (very happy because something fun is coming); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing excited: very happy because something fun is coming"},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows goodbye (what you say when you go away); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing goodbye: what you say when you go away"},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows classmate (a person in the same class as you); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing classmate: a person in the same class as you"},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Vocabulary Bingo”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Vocabulary Bingo"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U1-LS3-W01","script":"hungry. hungry. The hungry cat wants some fish.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U1-LS3-W02","script":"excited. excited. The boys are excited about the match.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U1-LS3-W03","script":"goodbye. goodbye. Say goodbye to Grandma.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U1-LS3-W04","script":"classmate. classmate. My classmate shares his crayons.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U1-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “How Do You Feel? Feelings and Greetings”. Let’s learn feeling words, opposites and greetings together. Meet some new words. hungry: you want to eat. excited: very happy because something fun is coming. goodbye: what you say when you go away. Feeling words tell us how someone is: happy, sad, tired, hungry, excited. We use them after am, is or are: I am hungry. Many words have an opposite: happy ↔ sad, hello ↔ goodbye. Learning words in pairs helps you remember them. Here are some examples. I am hungry. Can I have a sandwich? Lina is excited about the school trip. Goodbye, Mr. Khalid! See you tomorrow. Be careful! Some learners say: “I am boring in the lesson.” That’s not right. We say: “I am bored in the lesson.” bored = how you feel; boring = how the lesson is. Quick check: When do we say \"Good night\"? … Think! … When we leave at night or go to bed. Great job! Now you can say: I can say how I feel.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS4","title":"Capital Letters and Periods","objectives":["Students will be able to begin every sentence with a capital letter and end it with a period.","Students will be able to write I and people's names with capital letters.","I can start a sentence with a capital letter and end it with a period.","I can write I and names with a capital letter."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من بدء كل جملة بحرف كبير وإنهائها بنقطة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة I وأسماء الأشخاص بحرف كبير.","أستطيع أن أبدأ الجملة بحرف كبير وأنهيها بنقطة.","أستطيع أن أكتب I والأسماء بحرف كبير."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"hello","pos":"interjection","ipa":"/həˈloʊ/","definition":"a word you say when you meet someone","arabic":"مرحبًا","example":"Hello! Welcome to our class.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"name","pos":"noun","ipa":"/neɪm/","definition":"the word people call you","arabic":"اسم","example":"Her name is Noura.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"friend","pos":"noun","ipa":"/frɛnd/","definition":"a person you like and play with","arabic":"صديق","example":"Faisal is a good friend.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"happy","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈhæpi/","definition":"feeling good; smiling","arabic":"سعيد","example":"The happy boy is laughing.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"sad","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/sæd/","definition":"feeling bad; you want to cry","arabic":"حزين","example":"The girl is sad because it is raining.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"tired","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈtaɪɚd/","definition":"you want to rest or sleep","arabic":"متعب","example":"Dad is tired after work.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"In English, every sentence starts with a capital letter (A, B, C…) and ends with a period (.). In American English the dot at the end is called a period.\nThe word I is always a capital letter, even in the middle of a sentence. Names of people also start with a capital letter: Omar, Mr. Khalid.\nArabic has no capital letters, so this rule needs extra practice!\nStart every sentence with a capital letter: My bag is red.\nWrite I as a capital letter: Lina and I are friends.\nStart people's names with a capital letter: Yusuf, Noura, Mr. Khalid.\nEnd a telling sentence with a period: I am happy.","examples":["My friend is kind.","Yusuf and I are in the same class.","This is Ms. Huda.","She is my teacher.","I am excited today.","Adam is from Malaysia.","We are hungry.","Noura is my cousin."],"common_errors":["✗ my name is sara → ✓ My name is Sara. (Capital letter at the start and for names, and a period at the end.)","✗ yusuf and i are friends. → ✓ Yusuf and I are friends. (I is always a capital letter.)","✗ I am happy → ✓ I am happy. (Remember the period at the end.)"],"arabic":"لا توجد حروف كبيرة في العربية، لكن في الإنجليزية نبدأ كل جملة بحرف كبير.\nالضمير I (أنا) يُكتب دائمًا بحرف كبير، حتى في وسط الجملة.\nأسماء الأشخاص تبدأ بحرف كبير: Omar، ونضع النقطة (period) في نهاية الجملة الخبرية."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Capital Letters and Periods”. Let’s learn capital letters (sentence start, I, names) and periods together.","on_screen":"GV-L01-U1-LS4 | Capital Letters and Periods","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"In English, every sentence starts with a capital letter (A, B, C…) and ends with a period (.). In American English the dot at the end is called a period.","on_screen":"capital letters (sentence start, I, names) and periods","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"In English, every sentence starts with a capital letter (A, B, C…) and ends with a period (.). In American English the dot at the end is called a period. The word I is always a capital letter, even in the middle of a sentence. Names of people also start with a capital letter: Omar, Mr. Khalid.","on_screen":"Start every sentence with a capital letter: My bag is red. • Write I as a capital letter: Lina and I are friends. • Start people's names with a capital letter: Yusuf, Noura, Mr. Khalid.","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. My friend is kind. Yusuf and I are in the same class. This is Ms. Huda.","on_screen":"My friend is kind. / Yusuf and I are in the same class. / This is Ms. Huda.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “my name is sara.” That’s not right. We say: “My name is Sara.” Capital letter at the start and for names, and a period at the end.","on_screen":"✗ my name is sara   ✓ My name is Sara.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Is \"I\" ever a small letter in English? … Think! … No – \"I\" is always a capital letter. Great job! Now you can say: I can start a sentence with a capital letter and end it with a period.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can start a sentence with a capital letter and end it with a period.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: capital letters (sentence start, I, names) and periods.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","لا توجد حروف كبيرة في العربية، لكن في الإنجليزية نبدأ كل جملة بحرف كبير.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: my name is sara — الصحيح: My name is Sara.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أبدأ الجملة بحرف كبير وأنهيها بنقطة."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"About Me (editing passage)","body":"hello! My name is Faisal. I am nine years old My best friend is majed. He is funny. Majed and i are in Class 3C. we are happy at school.","word_count":30,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct sentence.","items":[{"q":"","options":["omar is my friend.","Omar is my friend","Omar is my friend.","omar Is my friend."],"answer":"Omar is my friend.","explanation":"Names of people start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"أسماء الأشخاص تبدأ بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["Lina and I are happy.","lina and i are happy.","Lina and I are happy","Lina and i are happy."],"answer":"Lina and I are happy.","explanation":"The word I is always a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"الضمير I يُكتب دائمًا بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["the cat is small.","the Cat is small.","The cat is small.","The cat is small"],"answer":"The cat is small.","explanation":"Start a sentence with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"ابدأ الجملة بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["This is Mr. khalid","This is mr. Khalid.","this is mr. khalid.","This is Mr. Khalid."],"answer":"This is Mr. Khalid.","explanation":"Names of people start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"أسماء الأشخاص تبدأ بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["We are tired","We are tired.","we are tired.","We Are tired"],"answer":"We are tired.","explanation":"End a telling sentence with a period (.).","explanation_ar":"أنهِ الجملة الخبرية بنقطة."},{"q":"","options":["My sister is Noura","My sister is noura.","my sister is noura.","My sister is Noura."],"answer":"My sister is Noura.","explanation":"Names of people start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"أسماء الأشخاص تبدأ بحرف كبير."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS4-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the mistake in each sentence.","items":[{"q":"yusuf is in Class 3A.","options":[],"answer":"Yusuf is in Class 3A.","explanation":"yusuf → Yusuf. Names of people start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: yusuf → Yusuf. أسماء الأشخاص تبدأ بحرف كبير."},{"q":"Adam and i are cousins.","options":[],"answer":"Adam and I are cousins.","explanation":"i → I. The word I is always a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: i → I. الضمير I يُكتب دائمًا بحرف كبير."},{"q":"my teacher is kind.","options":[],"answer":"My teacher is kind.","explanation":"my → My. Start a sentence with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: my → My. ابدأ الجملة بحرف كبير."},{"q":"Sara is excited","options":[],"answer":"Sara is excited.","explanation":"(add) → .. End a telling sentence with a period (.).","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → .. أنهِ الجملة الخبرية بنقطة."},{"q":"This is lina.","options":[],"answer":"This is Lina.","explanation":"lina → Lina. Names of people start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: lina → Lina. أسماء الأشخاص تبدأ بحرف كبير."},{"q":"the books are new.","options":[],"answer":"The books are new.","explanation":"the → The. Start a sentence with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: the → The. ابدأ الجملة بحرف كبير."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit the paragraph.","items":[{"q":"hello!","options":[],"answer":"Hello!","explanation":"hello → Hello. Start a sentence with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: hello → Hello. ابدأ الجملة بحرف كبير."},{"q":"I am nine years old My best friend is Majed.","options":[],"answer":"I am nine years old. My best friend is Majed.","explanation":"(add) → .. Start a sentence with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → .. ابدأ الجملة بحرف كبير."},{"q":"I am nine years old. My best friend is majed.","options":[],"answer":"I am nine years old. My best friend is Majed.","explanation":"majed → Majed. Start a sentence with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: majed → Majed. ابدأ الجملة بحرف كبير."},{"q":"Majed and i are in Class 3C. We are happy at school.","options":[],"answer":"Majed and I are in Class 3C. We are happy at school.","explanation":"i → I. Start a sentence with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: i → I. ابدأ الجملة بحرف كبير."},{"q":"Majed and I are in Class 3C. we are happy at school.","options":[],"answer":"Majed and I are in Class 3C. We are happy at school.","explanation":"we → We. Start a sentence with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: we → We. ابدأ الجملة بحرف كبير."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write it correctly.","items":[{"q":"Write 3 sentences about you and your friend. Use capital letters and periods.","options":[],"answer":"My name is Fahad. My friend is Ali. Ali and I are happy.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses capital letters (sentence start, I, names) and periods correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write the names of 3 people in your family with capital letters.","options":[],"answer":"Saad, Huda, Reem","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses capital letters (sentence start, I, names) and periods correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check your partner's sentences. Circle the capital letters and periods. Write one correction.","options":[],"answer":"“ali” → “Ali”","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses capital letters (sentence start, I, names) and periods correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Letter Ladder","mechanic":"word_builder","rules":["The leader chooses a word from the list and draws one blank line per letter.","Teams take turns guessing letters. Correct letters are written on the lines.","Each wrong guess removes one rung of the ladder (start with 6 rungs).","The team that completes the word scores 2 points and uses it in a sentence."],"data":[{"word":"hello","clue":"a word you say when you meet someone"},{"word":"name","clue":"the word people call you"},{"word":"friend","clue":"a person you like and play with"},{"word":"happy","clue":"feeling good; smiling"},{"word":"tired","clue":"you want to rest or sleep"},{"word":"teacher","clue":"a person who helps you learn at school"},{"word":"sad","clue":"feeling bad; you want to cry"},{"word":"student","clue":"a person who learns at school"},{"word":"hungry","clue":"you want to eat"},{"word":"excited","clue":"very happy because something fun is coming"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"","options":["reem Is my sister.","reem is my sister.","Reem is my sister.","Reem is my sister"],"answer":"Reem is my sister.","explanation":"Names of people start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"أسماء الأشخاص تبدأ بحرف كبير."},{"q":"Which words need a capital letter? \"my friend is yusuf.\"","options":["friend, is","my, yusuf","my, friend","is, yusuf"],"answer":"my, yusuf","explanation":"Names of people start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"أسماء الأشخاص تبدأ بحرف كبير."},{"q":"What goes at the end? \"We are in the classroom__\"","options":[".","'","-",","],"answer":".","explanation":"End a telling sentence with a period (.).","explanation_ar":"أنهِ الجملة الخبرية بنقطة."},{"q":"","options":["Faisal and i are friends.","faisal and I are friends.","Faisal and I are friends.","Faisal and I are friends"],"answer":"Faisal and I are friends.","explanation":"The word I is always a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"الضمير I يُكتب دائمًا بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["This is Ms. huda","this is ms. huda.","This is ms. Huda.","This is Ms. Huda."],"answer":"This is Ms. Huda.","explanation":"Names of people start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"أسماء الأشخاص تبدأ بحرف كبير."},{"q":"Which sentence is NOT correct?","options":["Adam and I are ten.","Adam is ten.","I am ten.","adam is ten."],"answer":"adam is ten.","explanation":"Names of people start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"أسماء الأشخاص تبدأ بحرف كبير."},{"q":"How do we write it correctly? \"i am hungry\"","options":["I am hungry.","I am Hungry.","i Am hungry","i am hungry."],"answer":"I am hungry.","explanation":"The word I is always a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"الضمير I يُكتب دائمًا بحرف كبير."},{"q":"How many letters must be capitals? \"omar and i are in class.\"","options":["0","2","3","1"],"answer":"2","explanation":"The word I is always a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"الضمير I يُكتب دائمًا بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["Noura is Happy today.","noura is happy today.","Noura is happy today","Noura is happy today."],"answer":"Noura is happy today.","explanation":"End a telling sentence with a period (.).","explanation_ar":"أنهِ الجملة الخبرية بنقطة."},{"q":"Which name is written correctly?","options":["Mr. khalid","mr. khalid","Mr. Khalid","mr. Khalid"],"answer":"Mr. Khalid","explanation":"Names of people start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"أسماء الأشخاص تبدأ بحرف كبير."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Hello, Friends!” that shows capital letters (sentence start, I, names) and periods in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Hello, Friends!” that shows capital letters (sentence start, I, names) and periods in action"},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Letter Ladder”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Letter Ladder"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U1-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Capital Letters and Periods”. Let’s learn capital letters (sentence start, I, names) and periods together. In English, every sentence starts with a capital letter (A, B, C…) and ends with a period (.). In American English the dot at the end is called a period. In English, every sentence starts with a capital letter (A, B, C…) and ends with a period (.). In American English the dot at the end is called a period. The word I is always a capital letter, even in the middle of a sentence. Names of people also start with a capital letter: Omar, Mr. Khalid. Here are some examples. My friend is kind. Yusuf and I are in the same class. This is Ms. Huda. Be careful! Some learners say: “my name is sara.” That’s not right. We say: “My name is Sara.” Capital letter at the start and for names, and a period at the end. Quick check: Is \"I\" ever a small letter in English? … Think! … No – \"I\" is always a capital letter. Great job! Now you can say: I can start a sentence with a capital letter and end it with a period.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS5","title":"All About Me: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to introduce themselves and a friend in speech and in writing.","Students will be able to use am/is/are, feeling words, capital letters and periods together.","I can introduce myself and a friend.","I can write an \"About Me\" card with correct capitals and periods."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من التعريف بأنفسهم وبصديق تحدثًا وكتابة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام am/is/are وكلمات المشاعر والحروف الكبيرة والنقطة معًا.","أستطيع أن أعرّف بنفسي وبصديقي.","أستطيع أن أكتب بطاقة «عنّي» بحروف كبيرة ونقاط صحيحة."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"hello","pos":"interjection","ipa":"/həˈloʊ/","definition":"a word you say when you meet someone","arabic":"مرحبًا","example":"Hello! Welcome to our class.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"name","pos":"noun","ipa":"/neɪm/","definition":"the word people call you","arabic":"اسم","example":"Her name is Noura.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"friend","pos":"noun","ipa":"/frɛnd/","definition":"a person you like and play with","arabic":"صديق","example":"Faisal is a good friend.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"happy","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈhæpi/","definition":"feeling good; smiling","arabic":"سعيد","example":"The happy boy is laughing.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"sad","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/sæd/","definition":"feeling bad; you want to cry","arabic":"حزين","example":"The girl is sad because it is raining.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"tired","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈtaɪɚd/","definition":"you want to rest or sleep","arabic":"متعب","example":"Dad is tired after work.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"teacher","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈtitʃɚ/","definition":"a person who helps you learn at school","arabic":"معلم","example":"Our teacher reads us a story.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"student","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈstudənt/","definition":"a person who learns at school","arabic":"طالب","example":"Every student has a new book.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"hungry","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈhʌŋɡri/","definition":"you want to eat","arabic":"جائع","example":"The hungry cat wants some fish.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"excited","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ɪkˈsaɪtəd/","definition":"very happy because something fun is coming","arabic":"متحمس","example":"The boys are excited about the match.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"goodbye","pos":"interjection","ipa":"/ˌɡʊdˈbaɪ/","definition":"what you say when you go away","arabic":"مع السلامة","example":"Say goodbye to Grandma.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"classmate","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈklæˌsmeɪt/","definition":"a person in the same class as you","arabic":"زميل الصف","example":"My classmate shares his crayons.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"In this lesson you use everything from Unit 1: am, is, are, feeling words, greetings, capital letters and periods.\nA good \"About Me\" card has a greeting, your name, your age, how you feel and a friend.\n✔ a greeting: Hello!\n✔ am, is or are in every sentence\n✔ one feeling word: happy, excited, tired…\n✔ capital letters and periods","examples":["Hello! I'm Fahad.","I am ten years old.","Today I am a little tired.","This is my friend Adam.","He is funny and kind.","We are in the same class.","Are you excited about the trip?","Goodbye, everyone!"],"common_errors":["✗ My friend he is Adam. → ✓ My friend is Adam. (Don't add he after the noun (Arabic: صديقي هو آدم).)","✗ I am 10 years. → ✓ I am 10 years old. (Say years old for age.)","✗ Hello my name is Fahad → ✓ Hello! My name is Fahad. (Put ! after Hello and start the next sentence with a capital letter.)"],"arabic":"في هذا الدرس نجمع كل ما تعلّمناه: am وis وare، وكلمات المشاعر، والتحيات، والحروف الكبيرة، والنقطة.\nلا نكرر الضمير بعد الاسم: My friend is Adam وليس My friend he is Adam.\nنقول العمر هكذا: I am ten years old."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “All About Me: Language in Use”. Let’s learn be, feeling words, greetings, capitals and periods (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L01-U1-LS5 | All About Me: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Meet and greet: walk around the class, say Hello, give your name, age and how you feel, ask \"Are you…?\" and say Goodbye.","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"In this lesson you use everything from Unit 1: am, is, are, feeling words, greetings, capital letters and periods. A good \"About Me\" card has a greeting, your name, your age, how you feel and a friend.","on_screen":"✔ a greeting: Hello! • ✔ am, is or are in every sentence • ✔ one feeling word: happy, excited, tired…","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Hello! I'm Fahad. I am ten years old. Today I am a little tired.","on_screen":"Hello! I'm Fahad. / I am ten years old. / Today I am a little tired.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “My friend he is Adam.” That’s not right. We say: “My friend is Adam.”","on_screen":"✗ My friend he is Adam.   ✓ My friend is Adam.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “I am 10 years.”? … Think! … It should be “I am 10 years old.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can introduce myself and a friend.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can introduce myself and a friend.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: be, feeling words, greetings, capitals and periods (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","في هذا الدرس نجمع كل ما تعلّمناه: am وis وare، وكلمات المشاعر، والتحيات، والحروف الكبيرة، والنقطة.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: My friend he is Adam. — الصحيح: My friend is Adam.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أعرّف بنفسي وبصديقي."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"About Me – Lina","body":"Hello! My name is Lina.\nI am eight years old.\nI am excited today because it is Art Day.\nMy best friend is Sara. She is kind and funny.\nWe are in Class 3B. Goodbye!","word_count":35,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U1-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Lina's card. True or False?","items":[{"q":"Lina is eight years old.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “About Me – Lina”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Lina is tired today.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “About Me – Lina”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Sara is Lina's best friend.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “About Me – Lina”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Sara is sad and angry.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “About Me – Lina”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Lina and Sara are in Class 3A.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “About Me – Lina”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"It is Art Day today.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “About Me – Lina”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"My cousins ___ in the garden.","options":["am","is","are","be"],"answer":"are","explanation":"Use am, is or are to match the subject.","explanation_ar":"استخدم am أو is أو are حسب الفاعل."},{"q":"___ your brother at home? – Yes, he is.","options":["Is","Are","Does","Am"],"answer":"Is","explanation":"Use am, is or are to match the subject.","explanation_ar":"استخدم am أو is أو are حسب الفاعل."},{"q":"It's 9 p.m. I want to sleep. I'm ___.","options":["hungry","tired","happy","excited"],"answer":"tired","explanation":"Choose the word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة ذات المعنى الصحيح."},{"q":"My friend ___ Majed.","options":["are","is","he is","am"],"answer":"is","explanation":"Don't repeat the subject with he or she after a noun.","explanation_ar":"لا تكرر الفاعل بضمير بعد الاسم."},{"q":"","options":["Majed and I are happy.","Majed and i are happy.","majed and i are happy.","Majed and I are happy"],"answer":"Majed and I are happy.","explanation":"Capital letter at the start, for I and for names; period at the end.","explanation_ar":"حرف كبير في البداية ومع I والأسماء، ونقطة في النهاية."},{"q":"How old is your brother? – He ___.","options":["has twelve years","is twelve years","twelve years old","is twelve years old"],"answer":"is twelve years old","explanation":"For age say: I am … years old.","explanation_ar":"للعمر نقول: I am … years old."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Speak, then write.","items":[{"q":"Say hello to your partner and ask his name. Write his answer.","options":[],"answer":"His name is Turki.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses be, feeling words, greetings, capitals and periods (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask: \"Are you tired today?\" Write the answer.","options":[],"answer":"No, he isn't. He is happy.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses be, feeling words, greetings, capitals and periods (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask: \"How old are you?\" Write the answer.","options":[],"answer":"He is nine years old.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses be, feeling words, greetings, capitals and periods (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask: \"Who is your best friend?\" Write the answer.","options":[],"answer":"His best friend is Nawaf.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses be, feeling words, greetings, capitals and periods (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Say goodbye in a polite way. Write it.","options":[],"answer":"Goodbye, Turki! See you tomorrow.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses be, feeling words, greetings, capitals and periods (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write your \"About Me\" card.","items":[{"q":"Plan: write notes – name, age, feeling, best friend.","options":[],"answer":"name: Fahad; age: 9; feeling: happy; friend: Ali","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses be, feeling words, greetings, capitals and periods (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write your card in 4–5 sentences. Use am, is and are.","options":[],"answer":"Hello! My name is Fahad. I am nine years old. I am happy today. My best friend is Ali. Goodbye!","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses be, feeling words, greetings, capitals and periods (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: capital letters? periods? am/is/are? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed “i am” to “I am”.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses be, feeling words, greetings, capitals and periods (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Treasure Hunt Review","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["Teams move to a station every 90 seconds.","At each station, write one correct sentence with the cue word and be, feeling words, greetings, capitals and periods (unit review).","Teams collect a \"treasure letter\" for each correct sentence.","Unscramble the letters at the end to reveal the secret word."],"data":[{"cue":"hello","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"name","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"friend","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"happy","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"sad","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"tired","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"teacher","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"student","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"hungry","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"excited","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"goodbye","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"classmate","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"Hello! I ___ Turki.","options":["are","is","am","be"],"answer":"am","explanation":"Use am, is or are to match the subject.","explanation_ar":"استخدم am أو is أو are حسب الفاعل."},{"q":"Adam and Yusuf ___ in the library.","options":["be","am","are","is"],"answer":"are","explanation":"Use am, is or are to match the subject.","explanation_ar":"استخدم am أو is أو are حسب الفاعل."},{"q":"___ the teacher in the classroom?","options":["Am","Be","Are","Is"],"answer":"Is","explanation":"Use am, is or are to match the subject.","explanation_ar":"استخدم am أو is أو are حسب الفاعل."},{"q":"The children aren't sad. They are smiling. They are ___.","options":["tired","sad","hungry","happy"],"answer":"happy","explanation":"Choose the word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة ذات المعنى الصحيح."},{"q":"It is 10 a.m. You see your teacher. You say:","options":["See you!","Good morning!","Good night!","Good evening!"],"answer":"Good morning!","explanation":"Choose the word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة ذات المعنى الصحيح."},{"q":"","options":["Ali my best friend.","Ali is my best friend.","Ali are my best friend.","Ali he is my best friend."],"answer":"Ali is my best friend.","explanation":"Don't repeat the subject with he or she after a noun.","explanation_ar":"لا تكرر الفاعل بضمير بعد الاسم."},{"q":"Are you ready? – ___","options":["Yes, I are.","Yes, I'm.","Yes, I am.","Yes, am I."],"answer":"Yes, I am.","explanation":"Use am, is or are to match the subject.","explanation_ar":"استخدم am أو is أو are حسب الفاعل."},{"q":"My sister ___ six years old.","options":["is","has","are","am"],"answer":"is","explanation":"For age say: I am … years old.","explanation_ar":"للعمر نقول: I am … years old."},{"q":"Which sentence needs a period at the end?","options":["Are you hungry?","My brother is funny","Goodbye, Adam!","Hello!"],"answer":"My brother is funny","explanation":"Capital letter at the start, for I and for names; period at the end.","explanation_ar":"حرف كبير في البداية ومع I والأسماء، ونقطة في النهاية."},{"q":"","options":["My friend and I are excited.","my friend and i are excited.","My friend and I excited.","My friend and I is excited."],"answer":"My friend and I are excited.","explanation":"Use am, is or are to match the subject.","explanation_ar":"استخدم am أو is أو are حسب الفاعل."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"Lina holding up a colorful \"About Me\" card with her photo, Sara clapping beside her in the girls' classroom. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Lina holding up a colorful \"About Me\" card with her photo, Sara clapping beside her in the girls' classroom"},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Hello, Friends!”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Hello, Friends!”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L01-U1-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Treasure Hunt Review”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Treasure Hunt Review"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U1-LS5-T1","script":"Hello! My name is Lina. I am eight years old. I am excited today because it is Art Day. My best friend is Sara. She is kind and funny. We are in Class 3B. Goodbye!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U1-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “All About Me: Language in Use”. Let’s learn be, feeling words, greetings, capitals and periods (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Meet and greet: walk around the class, say Hello, give your name, age and how you feel, ask \"Are you…?\" and say Goodbye. In this lesson you use everything from Unit 1: am, is, are, feeling words, greetings, capital letters and periods. A good \"About Me\" card has a greeting, your name, your age, how you feel and a friend. Here are some examples. Hello! I'm Fahad. I am ten years old. Today I am a little tired. Be careful! Some learners say: “My friend he is Adam.” That’s not right. We say: “My friend is Adam.” Quick check: what is wrong with “I am 10 years.”? … Think! … It should be “I am 10 years old.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can introduce myself and a friend.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"I ___ in Class 3A.","options":["be","am","are","is"],"answer":"am","explanation":"Use am with I.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم am مع I فقط."},{"q":"The teacher ___ in the office.","options":["be","am","is","are"],"answer":"is","explanation":"Use is with he, she, it or one person or thing.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم is مع he وshe وit أو مع المفرد."},{"q":"You and Sara ___ cousins.","options":["is","are","be","am"],"answer":"are","explanation":"Use are with you, we, they or two or more people or things.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم are مع you وwe وthey أو مع الجمع."},{"q":"My dog ___ black and white.","options":["is","am","are","have"],"answer":"is","explanation":"Use is with he, she, it or one person or thing.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم is مع he وshe وit أو مع المفرد."},{"q":"The boys ___ in the park.","options":["am","be","is","are"],"answer":"are","explanation":"Use are with you, we, they or two or more people or things.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم are مع you وwe وthey أو مع الجمع."},{"q":"My grandfather ___ seventy years old.","options":["are","is","has","am"],"answer":"is","explanation":"Use be (am/is/are) for age, not have.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم be للعمر وليس have."},{"q":"Ali ___ hungry. He is full.","options":["aren't","am not","isn't","not"],"answer":"isn't","explanation":"Negative: am / is / are + not (I'm not, isn't, aren't).","explanation_ar":"النفي: am أو is أو are ثم not."},{"q":"___ the girls in the garden?","options":["Be","Are","Am","Is"],"answer":"Are","explanation":"Question: put am, is or are first.","explanation_ar":"السؤال: نبدأ بـ am أو is أو are."},{"q":"Is your bag new? – No, it ___.","options":["is","not","aren't","isn't"],"answer":"isn't","explanation":"Short answers repeat the verb: Yes, she is. / No, she isn't.","explanation_ar":"الإجابة القصيرة تكرر الفعل."},{"q":"","options":["You are sleepy?","Is you sleepy?","Are you sleepy?","Are sleepy you?"],"answer":"Are you sleepy?","explanation":"Question: put am, is or are first.","explanation_ar":"السؤال: نبدأ بـ am أو is أو are."},{"q":"I want to eat. I am ___.","options":["tired","excited","hungry","bored"],"answer":"hungry","explanation":"Think about the meaning of the feeling word in the sentence.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في معنى كلمة الشعور في الجملة."},{"q":"Tomorrow is Eid! We are very ___.","options":["bored","tired","sad","excited"],"answer":"excited","explanation":"Think about the meaning of the feeling word in the sentence.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في معنى كلمة الشعور في الجملة."},{"q":"The opposite of \"sad\" is ___.","options":["tired","happy","angry","hungry"],"answer":"happy","explanation":"Opposites have opposite meanings (happy ↔ sad).","explanation_ar":"الأضداد كلمات معناها عكسي."},{"q":"You leave school at 1 p.m. You say:","options":["Good morning!","Goodbye!","Hello!","Good evening!"],"answer":"Goodbye!","explanation":"Choose the greeting that matches the time of day or the situation.","explanation_ar":"اختر التحية المناسبة للوقت أو الموقف."},{"q":"A ___ is a person in your class.","options":["classmate","cousin","neighbor","teacher"],"answer":"classmate","explanation":"Think about the meaning of the feeling word in the sentence.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في معنى كلمة الشعور في الجملة."},{"q":"The film is long and nothing happens. I am ___.","options":["excited","hungry","boring","bored"],"answer":"bored","explanation":"bored = the feeling; boring = the thing that makes you feel bored.","explanation_ar":"bored للشعور وboring للشيء."},{"q":"","options":["my Cousin is Hamad.","My cousin is hamad.","My cousin is Hamad.","my cousin is hamad."],"answer":"My cousin is Hamad.","explanation":"Names of people start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"أسماء الأشخاص تبدأ بحرف كبير."},{"q":"Which words need capital letters? \"hamad and i are friends.\"","options":["hamad, i","are, friends","friends, i","and, are"],"answer":"hamad, i","explanation":"The word I is always a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"الضمير I يُكتب دائمًا بحرف كبير."},{"q":"What is missing? \"My teacher is kind\"","options":["a period at the end","a comma","a capital M","a question mark"],"answer":"a period at the end","explanation":"End a telling sentence with a period (.).","explanation_ar":"أنهِ الجملة الخبرية بنقطة."},{"q":"","options":["Saad and I are in the garden","saad and I are in the garden.","Saad and I are in the garden.","Saad and i are in the garden."],"answer":"Saad and I are in the garden.","explanation":"The word I is always a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"الضمير I يُكتب دائمًا بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["This is Ms. reem.","this is Ms. Reem.","This is ms. reem.","This is Ms. Reem."],"answer":"This is Ms. Reem.","explanation":"Names of people start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"أسماء الأشخاص تبدأ بحرف كبير."},{"q":"Complete Fahad's card: \"Hello! My name is Fahad. ___\"","options":["I have nine years.","I is nine years old.","I nine years old.","I am nine years old."],"answer":"I am nine years old.","explanation":"Use be (am/is/are) for age, not have.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم be للعمر وليس have."},{"q":"How can we fix this sentence? \"Omar he is my friend.\"","options":["Omar is my friend.","He Omar is my friend.","Omar he are my friend.","Omar my friend."],"answer":"Omar is my friend.","explanation":"Don't repeat the subject with he or she after a noun.","explanation_ar":"لا تكرر الفاعل بضمير بعد الاسم."},{"q":"Are your friends happy? – ___","options":["Yes, they are.","Yes, they're.","Yes, they is.","Yes, are they."],"answer":"Yes, they are.","explanation":"Positive short answers use the full form: Yes, I am.","explanation_ar":"الإجابة القصيرة بالإيجاب لا تُختصر."}],"theme_ar":"مرحبًا يا أصدقاء!","essential_question_ar":"كيف نُخبر الناس مَن نحن؟","can_do":"I can say who I am, how old I am and how I feel using am, is and are.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أقول مَن أنا وكم عمري وكيف أشعر باستخدام am وis وare."});
